<title>USA: Union Acceptance gets $65 million in debt.</title>
<headline>Union Acceptance gets $65 million in debt.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Acceptance Corp said Friday it reached an agreement with private investors on the issuance of $65 million in senior unsecured debt.</p>
<p>The company said funding is expected on Monday, March 24.</p>
<p>The debt was issued at 135 basis points over the relevant treasury, and is the most successful for the company to date, Union Acceptance said. It has a 5.5 year average life and an effective coupon rate of 7.8 percent.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
